                            Variant: 16 (2, 1)


                                   ABOUT
                                   =====

This repo is related to web development class.


                               INSTALLATION
                               ============

One have to install some software. Following dependencies can be obtained
from package manager or their official site.

    1) git (https://git-scm.com/);
    2) NodeJS (https://nodejs.org/);
    3) PostgreSQL (https://www.postgresql.org/).

To deploy this project one should follow these steps:

    1) Clone `develop' branch of the repository:
        $ git clone -b develop https://github.com/gdcdec/weblab6

    2) Jump to backend directory:
        $ cd weblab6/backend

    3) Intall NodeJS dependencies specified in package.json:
        $ npm install --omit=dev

       --omit=dev flag is required to parry installation of packages
       specified in devDependencies section of package.json. By default,
       `npm install' installs all modules listed both in `dependecies'
       and `devDependencies' of package.json.

    4) Create `.env' file inside backend directory:

        DB_NAME=
        DB_USER=
        DB_PASSWORD=
        DB_HOST=
        DB_PORT=
        DATABASE_DIALECT=postgres

       Fill in the right sides with necessary values.

    5) Create database with the same name as mentioned in `.env' file.

    6) Run server in development mode:
        $ npm run dev


                                   USAGE
                                   =====

Graphical user interface is not implemented yet. To obtain current functionality
one can use curl to make a request to the server:

    * Get test response:
        $ curl -X GET localhost:3000

    * Get all users:
        $ curl -X GET -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept: application/json" http://localhost:3000/users

    * Create new user:
        $ curl -X POST -d '{ "name": "John Smith", "email": "john.smith@example.com" }' -H "Content-Type: application/json" http://localhost:3000/users

    * Get all events:
        $ curl -X GET -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept: application/json" http://localhost:3000/events

    * Get event by its id:
        $ curl -X GET -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Accept: application/json" http://localhost:3000/events/<evenID>

    * Create new event:
        $ curl -X POST -d '{ "title": "New Event", "description": "Description for new event", "date": "2025-03-15T14:00:00.000Z", "createdBy": 1 }' -H "Content-Type: application/json" http://localhost:3000/events

    * Update event by its id:
        $ curl -X PUT -d '{ "title": "Updated Event", "description": "Description for updated event", "date": "2025-12-12T14:00:00.000Z", "createdBy": 1 }' -H "Content-Type: application/json" http://localhost:3000/events/<eventID>

    * Delete event by its id:
        $ curl -X DELETE -H "Content-Type: application/json" http://localhost:3000/events/<eventID>
